public newBundle([String](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/String.html "class in java.lang") baseName, [Locale](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Locale.html "class in java.util") locale, [String](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/String.html "class in java.lang") format, [ClassLoader](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/ClassLoader.html "class in java.lang") loader, boolean reload) throws [IllegalAccessException](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/IllegalAccessException.html "class in java.lang"), [InstantiationException](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/InstantiationException.html "class in java.lang"), [IOException](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/io/IOException.html "class in java.io")
Instantiates a resource bundle for the given bundle name of the given format and locale, using the given class loader if necessary. This method returns `null` if there is no resource bundle available for the given parameters. If a resource bundle can't be instantiated due to an unexpected error, the error must be reported by throwing an `Error` or `Exception` rather than simply returning `null`. 
If the `reload` flag is `true`, it indicates that this method is being called because the previously loaded resource bundle has expired. 

Implementation Requirements:
    Resource bundles in named modules are subject to the encapsulation rules specified by [`Module.getResourceAsStream`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/Module.html#getResourceAsStream\(java.lang.String\)). A resource bundle in a named module visible to the given class loader is accessible when the package of the resource file corresponding to the resource bundle is open unconditionally. 
The default implementation instantiates a `ResourceBundle` as follows. 
      * The bundle name is obtained by calling [`toBundleName(baseName,  locale)`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/ResourceBundle.Control.html#toBundleName\(java.lang.String,java.util.Locale\)).
      * If `format` is `"java.class"`, the [`Class`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/Class.html "class in java.lang") specified by the bundle name is loaded with the given class loader. If the `Class` is found and accessible then the `ResourceBundle` is instantiated. The resource bundle is accessible if the package of the bundle class file is open unconditionally; otherwise, `IllegalAccessException` will be thrown. Note that the `reload` flag is ignored for loading class-based resource bundles in this default implementation. 
      * If `format` is `"java.properties"`, [`toResourceName(bundlename,  "properties")`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/ResourceBundle.Control.html#toResourceName\(java.lang.String,java.lang.String\)) is called to get the resource name. If `reload` is `true`, [`load.getResource`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/ClassLoader.html#getResource\(java.lang.String\)) is called to get a [`URL`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/net/URL.html "class in java.net") for creating a [`URLConnection`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/net/URLConnection.html "class in java.net"). This `URLConnection` is used to [disable the caches](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/net/URLConnection.html#setUseCaches\(boolean\)) of the underlying resource loading layers, and to [get an `InputStream`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/net/URLConnection.html#getInputStream\(\)). Otherwise, [`loader.getResourceAsStream`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/ClassLoader.html#getResourceAsStream\(java.lang.String\)) is called to get an [`InputStream`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/io/InputStream.html "class in java.io"). Then, a [`PropertyResourceBundle`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/PropertyResourceBundle.html "class in java.util") is constructed with the `InputStream`.
      * If `format` is neither `"java.class"` nor `"java.properties"`, an `IllegalArgumentException` is thrown.
      * If the `locale`'s language is one of the [Legacy language codes](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Locale.html#legacy_language_codes), either old or new, then repeat the loading process if needed, with the bundle name with the other language. For example, "iw" for "he" and vice versa.  

Parameters:
     `baseName` - the base bundle name of the resource bundle, a fully qualified class name      `locale` - the locale for which the resource bundle should be instantiated      `format` - the resource bundle format to be loaded      `loader` - the `ClassLoader` to use to load the bundle      `reload` - the flag to indicate bundle reloading; `true` if reloading an expired resource bundle, `false` otherwise 

Returns:
    the resource bundle instance, or `null` if none could be found. 

Throws:
     `NullPointerException[](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/NullPointerException.html "class in java.lang")` - if `bundleName`, `locale`, `format`, or `loader` is `null`, or if `null` is returned by [`toBundleName`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/ResourceBundle.Control.html#toBundleName\(java.lang.String,java.util.Locale\))      `IllegalArgumentException[](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/IllegalArgumentException.html "class in java.lang")` - if `format` is unknown, or if the resource found for the given parameters contains malformed data.      - if the loaded class cannot be cast to `ResourceBundle`      `IllegalAccessException[](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/IllegalAccessException.html "class in java.lang")` - if the class or its nullary constructor is not accessible.      `InstantiationException[](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/InstantiationException.html "class in java.lang")` - if the instantiation of a class fails for some other reason.      `ExceptionInInitializerError[](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/ExceptionInInitializerError.html "class in java.lang")` - if the initialization provoked by this method fails.      - if an error occurred when reading resources using any I/O operations 

